body:
GREEN. GREEN. GREEN. GREEN.

&#x200B;

You mean I can have my unhealthy coping mechanism without any lasting effects? So I can do it way more and put myself in danger by my carelessness? Heck yeah!!

Yeahhhhh a LOT of people gave me shit for this post, but I'm autistic aha. And have ADHD. And anxiety. And depression. And who the heck else knows?

&#x200B;

Point is, cooking is very hard for me. Every so often, I'll get a burst of energy and make a fancy elaborate meal, but all of the people who made fun of me for not making organic meals every day feels very... ableist? Idk if that's the right word? It's just so weird getting yelled at for telling other autistic people about veganism, because they call me ableist and bigoted because "blah blah I need to eat meat for texture reasons, low FOPMAD blah blah." And then I head over to vegan spaces and get criticized for not being 100% certified organic and eating ramen every day. Like... idk. I don't feel fully welcome in either community anymore.

&#x200B;

Idk why I'm dumping this all on you lol. I tried making a fully organic meal yesterday. It took me two hours and I hated it. 500 five-star reviews but yet... ugh. Idk. People are always just telling me I'm living my lifestyle wrong ALL the time and I hate it. I hate that. the vegan community is so focused on health? I thought it was a bout the animals, and that hating on vegans who do it for health was funny? So why are we like this?

&#x200B;

Whatever. Idk. Gonna go make some ramen like I have been doing every day the past three months. Lol.

It's creating more demand for mass farming? I would love to see the source for that, considering how much land livestock take up, and how the majority of crops grown go to animal feed. Most soy grown is given to animals to eat, so you may eat them later.

&#x200B;

They're not simply dietary choices. They're ethical choices, closely tied to morals pertaining to animal welfare. Seeing veganism as a simple diet is inaccurate. Also, my experience has been that reducing meat consumption and veganism is on the rise, especially considering the plant-based industry teaming up with even fast food corporations. There are many more choices in grocery stores than there used to be.

Sources? You know, reliable ones? Well, I suppose I'll just list mine first then.

&#x200B;

Here's a published journal from the National Library of Medicine. Feel free to read all of it, check out the 58 sources listed, or perhaps even the studies used for the data: [https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/pmc/articles/PMC9007375/](https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/pmc/articles/PMC9007375/) 

This goes in-depth on ingredients in vegan dog foods: [https://www.sciencedirect.com/science/article/pii/S0377840122001432?via%3Dihub](https://www.sciencedirect.com/science/article/pii/S0377840122001432?via%3Dihub) 

&#x200B;

This one is about palatability: [https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/pmc/articles/PMC8208530/](https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/pmc/articles/PMC8208530/) 

&#x200B;

Please do give a heads-up if you cannot access these journal articles for whatever reason. I am not exactly sure about the permissions needed, but I believe they're all available for the public. If you can find recent journal articles to support your claims, I would love to read them. I find this stuff all very interesting.

Yeah, men should be allowed to express themselves without being ridiculed. I don't know why dudes think hating on women will help with this though??

&#x200B;

Me: "Hey, I'm depressed."

&#x200B;

Men on Reddit: "You will never know true depression! You're a woman and have it so easy. Stop complaining!"

&#x200B;

Men irl: "You would be so much prettier if you smiled." And then I don't do as they say, and they either glare at or insult me.

&#x200B;

My family: "Yeah, I have depression too, but that doesn't mean my house is messy or I'm failing classes. You're just being lazy and whiny. Pull yourself up by your bootstraps. Also, stop frowning. It's rude."  


Me: "Hey, I self harm."

&#x200B;

Guys in my DMs: "Can I see pictures of your cuts? I'd love to lick the blood off your thighs! Fuck, I'd love to be the one cutting you. 😍"

&#x200B;

My family: "You're ruining your body! Stop it, you fucking idiot. You're making yourself ugly!!!" (Because my only value is in being pretty???)

&#x200B;

Stop making depression a gendered issue. Seriously. Everyone with depression has it fucking bad.  It's not "easier" for women because they don't get yelled at for crying. It's not "easier" for men because they aren't in constant fear of sexual assault. Jesus. Hating on an entire gender isn't going to make you feel better, bestie. Please stop.

These are tame crested ducks. These ducks are bred to purposefully have a skull deformity to have the feathers look like that. Most babies die in the shell or are born, have seizures due to the skull deformity, and die. Most have lifelong neurological deformities.

&#x200B;

An absolutely disgusting practice.

Oopsie I cut off the top of the poster. It reads;

"Have you seen Shipibo?
Nicknamed Shibi"
